      "text": "First, we need to determine the cost of the painting in Namibian dollars (ND). We know that:\n1 US dollar (US$) = 7 Namibian dollars (ND)\n\nGiven that the painting costs 105 Namibian dollars, we can express this as:\n\\[ 105 \\text{ ND} = 105 \\text{ ND} \\]\n\nNext, we need to convert the cost of the painting from Namibian dollars to Chinese yuan (CNY). We know that:\n1 US dollar (US$) = 6 Chinese yuan (CNY)\n\nSince 1 US dollar = 7 Namibian dollars, we can find the cost of the painting in US dollars by dividing the cost of the painting in Namibian dollars by the conversion rate:\n\\[ \\text{Cost in US dollars} = \\frac{105 \\text{ ND}}{7} = 15 \\text{ US$} \\]\n\nNow, we convert the cost from US dollars to Chinese yuan. Since 1 US dollar = 6 Chinese yuan:\n\\[ \\text{Cost in Chinese yuan} = 15 \\text{ US$} \\times 6 \\text{ CNY/US$} = 90 \\text{ CNY} \\]\n\nTherefore, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is:\n\\[ \\boxed{90} \\]",
