      "text": "First, we need to convert the cost of the painting from Namibian dollars to US dollars. We know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 7 Namibian dollars, so to find out how many US dollars the painting costs, we divide the cost in Namibian dollars by 7:\n\\[ \\text{Cost in US dollars} = \\frac{105 \\text{ Namibian dollars}}{7 \\text{ Namibian dollars/US dollar}} = 15 \\text{ US dollars} \\]\nNext, we need to convert the cost from US dollars to Chinese yuan. We know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 6 Chinese yuan, so to find out how many Chinese yuan the painting costs, we multiply the cost in US dollars by 6:\n\\[ \\text{Cost in Chinese yuan} = 15 \\text{ US dollars} \\times 6 \\text{ yuan/US dollar} = 90 \\text{ Chinese yuan} \\]\nTherefore, the painting would cost $\\boxed{90}$ Chinese yuan.",
